@page "/docs/components/hover-card"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.HoverCard
<PageTitle>Hover Card - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Hover Card</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="hover-card" />
        </div>
        <p>A rich preview that opens when a trigger such as a link or avatar is hovered or focused, positioned with <a class="font-medium text-foreground" href="https://floating-ui.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floating UI</a>. Unlike a tooltip, the card is <strong>interactive</strong>: a close delay gives the pointer time to move onto it. It is also <strong>non-modal</strong>, so the rest of the page stays usable, and Escape or a click outside dismisses it.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(HoverCardUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, add a trigger and a content card. With `RenderAs`, any element can act as the trigger." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a hover card. The trigger and content share one `BzHoverCard` root, and an optional `BzHoverCardArrow` inside the content points back at the trigger." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="A profile preview behind a username link. Hover or focus the link, then move onto the card to interact with it. Leaving both closes the card after a short delay."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger (RenderAs)" Description="Use `RenderAs` to make your own element the trigger instead of the default button. Here an anchor receives `p.Attributes`."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arrow" Description="Add a `BzHoverCardArrow` inside the content to point at the trigger. It shares the card's fill, ring and shadow so it reads as part of the card, and it turns to face whichever side the card opens on."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardArrowExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Alignment" Description="`Align` places the card along the trigger's edge, at the start, center or end."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardAlignExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sides" Description="`Side` sets the preferred edge for the card: left, top, bottom or right. When there isn't room, it flips to the opposite side."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardSideExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Open &amp; close delays" Description="`OpenDelay` is how long the pointer must rest on the trigger before the card opens, and `CloseDelay` is how long the card stays after the pointer leaves. One card here opens instantly and the other takes its time."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardDelayExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind `Open` when your code needs to know or set the state. The value shown above stays in sync as you hover the trigger, move onto the card or dismiss it."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="Every part accepts `Class`. This example gives the trigger link a brand color and the card a custom width, radius, tint and ring."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the card's placement and alignment mirror and its content reads right to left."
          Example="typeof(HoverCardRtlExample)" />

</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzHoverCard",
        new CompositionNode("BzHoverCardTrigger"),
        new CompositionNode("BzHoverCardContent",
            new CompositionNode("BzHoverCardArrow")));
}
